DOMAIN: Configuration & Environment Variables
FILES: src/db_monitor/core/config/__init__.py (settings singleton), src/db_monitor/core/config/dataclasses/ (core.py, db.py, auth_settings.py, broker.py, ingestion.py, observability.py, retention.py, webhook.py, backplane.py, validation.py, factory.py), src/db_monitor/core/config/normalizers/ (quotas.py, slo.py, urls.py), src/db_monitor/core/config/normalizers/clusters/ (defaults.py, loader.py, normalizers.py), src/db_monitor/core/config_loader.py (get_env_or_file, parse_csv_list, config_error, default_schema_mode), src/db_monitor/core/config/loaders.py (re-exports only)
NOTE: There is no flat config module and no module-level constants. Config is a validated dataclass tree: use `from db_monitor.core.config import settings` and read nested fields (`settings.db.postgres_url`, `settings.auth.jwt_secret`, `settings.broker.kafka_topics`, `settings.observability.otel_exporter`). Never import `POSTGRES_URL`/`JWT_SECRET`/`DB_POOL_SIZE` — those names no longer exist.
ENTRY: `settings = _get_settings()` runs at import of db_monitor.core.config → `AppSettings.from_env()` (cached once, validated). Env vars are read at import time.

SETTINGS TREE (attribute ← env var, default):
- AppSettings (core.py): env ← APP_ENV (development); db_schema_mode ← DB_SCHEMA_MODE (apply in dev, validate in prod); app_shutdown_timeout_seconds ← APP_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (45); readiness_max_commit_age_seconds ← READINESS_MAX_COMMIT_AGE_SECONDS (300); readiness_max_consumer_lag ← READINESS_MAX_CONSUMER_LAG (1000); readiness_max_dlq_messages ← READINESS_MAX_DLQ_MESSAGES (0); slo_rolling_window_days ← SLO_ROLLING_WINDOW_DAYS (30); tenant_cohort_slo_policies ← TENANT_COHORT_SLO_POLICIES (JSON)
- settings.db (db.py): postgres_url ← POSTGRES_URL (postgresql+asyncpg://postgres:postgres@localhost:5437/postgres); sqlalchemy_echo ← SQLALCHEMY_ECHO; pool_size ← DB_POOL_SIZE (10); max_overflow ← DB_MAX_OVERFLOW (20); pool_timeout_seconds ← DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (30); pool_recycle_seconds ← DB_POOL_RECYCLE_SECONDS (1800); pool_pre_ping ← DB_POOL_PRE_PING (true)
- settings.auth (auth_settings.py): jwt_secret ← JWT_SECRET; jwt_secret_next ← JWT_SECRET_NEXT; jwt_algorithm ← JWT_ALGORITHM (HS256); access_token_ttl_minutes ← ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL_MINUTES (15); ws_session_token_ttl_seconds ← WS_SESSION_TOKEN_TTL_SECONDS (60); api_key_default_ttl_days ← API_KEY_DEFAULT_TTL_DAYS (90); allow_bootstrap ← ALLOW_BOOTSTRAP; ws_backplane_enabled ← WS_BACKPLANE_ENABLED (true); ws_backplane_channel ← WS_BACKPLANE_CHANNEL (db_monitor_ws_events)
- settings.broker (broker.py): message_broker ← MESSAGE_BROKER (kafka); dlq_enabled ← DLQ_ENABLED (true); batch_enabled ← BATCH_ENABLED (true); batch_size ← BATCH_SIZE (100); kafka_broker ← KAFKA_BROKER (kafka:9092); kafka_security_protocol ← KAFKA_SECURITY_PROTOCOL (PLAINTEXT); kafka_ssl_cafile/certfile/keyfile/password ← KAFKA_SSL_*; kafka_topic ← KAFKA_TOPIC (orderdb.public.orders); kafka_consumer_group ← KAFKA_CONSUMER_GROUP (fastapi-consumer-group); rabbitmq_url ← RABBITMQ_URL; rabbitmq_queue ← RABBITMQ_QUEUE (db-monitor-events); rabbitmq_prefetch_count ← RABBITMQ_PREFETCH_COUNT (100); rabbitmq_dlq_queue ← RABBITMQ_DLQ_QUEUE (db-monitor-dlq)
- settings.backplane (backplane.py): backend ← WS_BACKPLANE_BACKEND (postgres|redis); redis_url ← REDIS_URL; redis_channel_prefix ← REDIS_BACKPLANE_CHANNEL_PREFIX (db_monitor)
- settings.ingestion (ingestion.py): quota_enabled ← INGESTION_QUOTA_ENABLED (false); quota_window_seconds ← INGESTION_QUOTA_WINDOW_SECONDS (60); source_default_events_per_window ← INGESTION_SOURCE_DEFAULT_EVENTS_PER_WINDOW (0=unlimited); tenant_default_events_per_window ← INGESTION_TENANT_DEFAULT_EVENTS_PER_WINDOW (0); quota_mode ← INGESTION_QUOTA_MODE (throttle|drop); quota_max_throttle_seconds ← INGESTION_QUOTA_MAX_THROTTLE_SECONDS (5.0); bulk_write_enabled ← INGESTION_BULK_WRITE_ENABLED (true)
- settings.observability (observability.py): otel_tracing_enabled ← OTEL_TRACING_ENABLED (false); otel_service_name ← OTEL_SERVICE_NAME (db-monitor); otel_exporter ← OTEL_EXPORTER (otlp|console); otel_exporter_otlp_endpoint/headers ← OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT/HEADERS; audit_log_queue_maxsize ← AUDIT_LOG_QUEUE_MAXSIZE (10000); audit_log_batch_size ← AUDIT_LOG_BATCH_SIZE (100); audit_log_flush_interval_seconds ← AUDIT_LOG_FLUSH_INTERVAL_SECONDS (1.0); audit_log_queue_mode ← AUDIT_LOG_QUEUE_MODE (drop|block|spill)
- settings.retention (retention.py): cleanup_enabled ← RETENTION_CLEANUP_ENABLED (false); cleanup_interval_seconds ← RETENTION_CLEANUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS (3600); cleanup_batch_size ← RETENTION_CLEANUP_BATCH_SIZE (1000); cleanup_max_batches_per_table ← RETENTION_CLEANUP_MAX_BATCHES_PER_TABLE (10); archive_before_delete ← RETENTION_ARCHIVE_BEFORE_DELETE; archive_dir ← RETENTION_ARCHIVE_DIR (retention-archive); event_retention_days ← EVENT_RETENTION_DAYS (30); column_changes_retention_days ← COLUMN_CHANGES_RETENTION_DAYS (30); dead_letter_retention_days ← DEAD_LETTER_RETENTION_DAYS (30); api_audit_log_retention_days ← API_AUDIT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS (90); spill_retention_days ← SPILL_RETENTION_DAYS (30)
- settings.webhook (webhook.py): urls ← WEBHOOK_URLS (CSV); timeout_seconds ← WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS (5.0); shared_secret ← WEBHOOK_SHARED_SECRET; max_retries ← WEBHOOK_MAX_RETRIES (3); retry_backoff_seconds ← WEBHOOK_RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS (0.5); circuit_breaker_threshold ← WEBHOOK_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_THRESHOLD (5); circuit_breaker_recovery_seconds ← WEBHOOK_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_RECOVERY_SECONDS (30.0)

COMPUTED FIELDS (populated in factory.py after construction):
- broker.kafka_topics ← KAFKA_TOPICS CSV, else [kafka_topic]
- broker.rabbitmq_queues ← RABBITMQ_QUEUES CSV, else [rabbitmq_queue]
- broker.kafka_ssl_context ← built when protocol is SSL/SASL_SSL
- broker.kafka_clusters ← load_kafka_clusters(); broker.broker_clusters ← load_broker_clusters() (BROKER_CLUSTERS supersedes KAFKA_CLUSTERS)
- ingestion.source_quotas ← INGESTION_SOURCE_QUOTAS JSON; ingestion.tenant_quotas ← INGESTION_TENANT_QUOTAS JSON
- webhook.urls ← WEBHOOK_URLS CSV

SECRETS: get_env_or_file(name, default) reads NAME, then NAME_FILE (file contents, stripped). A missing NAME_FILE path raises config_error. Use the _FILE variant for Docker/K8s secrets (JWT_SECRET_FILE, POSTGRES_URL_FILE, RABBITMQ_URL_FILE, WEBHOOK_SHARED_SECRET_FILE, KAFKA_SSL_PASSWORD_FILE, REDIS_URL_FILE, DB_SCHEMA_MODE_FILE).

VALIDATION (validation.py, runs inside from_env()):
- DB_SCHEMA_MODE ∈ {apply, validate, skip}
- APP_ENV=production|prod adds hardening: DB_POOL_SIZE>=1, DB_MAX_OVERFLOW>=0, DB_POOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS>=1, DB_POOL_RECYCLE_SECONDS>=0, POSTGRES_URL not the default localhost DSN, JWT_SECRET set and >=32 chars (JWT_SECRET_NEXT also >=32 if set), ALLOW_BOOTSTRAP forced off unless the env var is present
- OTEL_EXPORTER ∈ {otlp, console}; tracing + otlp requires OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
- WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT_SECONDS>0, MAX_RETRIES>=0, RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS>=0, CIRCUIT_BREAKER_THRESHOLD>=1, recovery>0, every URL starts http:// or https://
- MESSAGE_BROKER ∈ {kafka, rabbitmq}; RABBITMQ_PREFETCH_COUNT>0
- INGESTION_QUOTA_WINDOW_SECONDS>0, default limits>=0, QUOTA_MODE ∈ {throttle, drop}, MAX_THROTTLE_SECONDS>0
- SLO_ROLLING_WINDOW_DAYS>0; retention interval/batch/max-batches>0 and all *_DAYS>=0

PITFALLS:
- settings is built once at import of db_monitor.core.config. Changing os.environ afterwards has no effect — restart the process, or monkeypatch the settings object in tests.
- Attribute names are lowercase and nested (settings.db.pool_size), not SCREAMING_SNAKE env-var names.
- BROKER_CLUSTERS and KAFKA_CLUSTERS are mutually exclusive; BROKER_CLUSTERS wins.
- JWT_SECRET_NEXT enables zero-downtime rotation; both secrets are tried during decode.
- ws_backplane_enabled lives on settings.auth, but the backend/Redis knobs live on settings.backplane.

